    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0866" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/11583</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-15T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 15, 1917, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.35 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5699. Your 4432, February 13 [12]. Foreign Office reply is as follows:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>It is prepared to grant permits for export of German needles specified in
                        exhibits one to five. “In order, however, to enable me to give the necessary
                        instructions for the issue of the permit, I have the honour to enquire
                        whether I could be supplied with a list setting forth clearly the exact
                        quantity and the value of smooth needles for which a permit is desired. It
                        has proved difficult to ascertain from the exhibits whether all smooth
                        needles shown therein are now awaiting shipment.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Exhibits are being returned to Department by next bag.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
